  },
  "locales": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Plural and inclusive pronouns",
      "summary": "English has one we, which may or may not include the listener.",
      "status": "draft",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "What it is",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "We, you and they are the plural pronouns. Some languages have two words for we: one that includes the listener and one that does not. English has only one."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**We** are friends.",
                "Do **you** all agree?",
                "**They** live next door."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "How it works in English",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "The English we can include or exclude the listener, and the context decides. To be clear, add a phrase such as all of us, both of us or you and I."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "html": "<table><thead><tr><th>Meaning</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>listener included</td><td><strong>We should all go.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>listener excluded</td><td><strong>We are leaving; you stay.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>made clear</td><td><strong>all of us, both of us</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
